  "honestLimits": [
    "A stamp attests that validators agreed the evidence page references the event. It is not cryptographic proof of physical presence.",
    "Evidence must be a public https page. Event dates are supplied by the claimer. Stamps, once added, are never overwritten.",
    "The last-30-days count is measured from the passport most recent stamp date, because the chain has no wall clock.",
    "The contract holds no funds and no escrow.",
    "Real extension-wallet signing, real-device rendering, and a UI-driven fresh claim flow were not personally verified in this build; the write paths were proven end-to-end by script to FINALIZED and read back.",
