  "receiptShapeNote": "On this network, a UserError rejection finalizes as ERROR with an empty .error field; the guard code is carried in leader_receipt[0].result.payload (for example DUPLICATE_CLAIM), and SUCCESS steps carry a null result payload. Guard proofs therefore rest on FINALIZED status, the payload code, and state readbacks showing no change.",
  "contractRegistrationNote": "The contract class must subclass gl.Contract. @allow_storage alone only marks the class for storage use; it does not register the class as the contract, and the GenVM runner then fails deployment with no contract defined. Local direct tests do not enforce this, so they cannot prove Studionet acceptance on this point."
}